# This repository deliberately keeps mixed line endings per file (most files are LF; README.md,
# AGENTS.md, LICENSE.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/ROADMAP.md, docs/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md and a few
# others are CRLF). Golden hashes, source-rule tests and byte-identical artefacts depend on the bytes
# in the working tree being the bytes in the index, so Git must never convert line endings on
# checkout or commit, whatever core.autocrlf says on the machine.
* -text

# Better hunk headers in diffs; these do not change file contents.
*.md diff=markdown
*.cs diff=csharp
